Composite Pattern means modeling simple objects and composite objects (like group obj)
with a common interface so that both can be treated uniformly.

it means we have same functionalities on these obj (render() on shape & group)
we create an interface above them,
and instead some condition to find witch type
use polymorphism on Group!

Note:  composite object is an object that can contain itself and other objects
       like folder, like group obj on PowerPoint
       so it can be have limitless nested relationships
       it's the reason, we need recursive logic

Note: if we want to add new functionalities (like move, delete)
      we should add them on Component Interface
      because they should use on every obj on the hierarchy!

            +------------------+
            |    Component     |
            |------------------|
            | + render()       |
            +------------------+
                  /_\
                   |
         -----------------------
         |                     |
 +------------------+   +----------------------+
 |       Shape      |   |         Group        |
 |------------------|   |----------------------|
 | + render()       |   | - List<Component>    |
 +------------------+   | + render()           |
                        | + add()              |
                        +----------------------+


 GOF UML:
           +------------------+
           |    Component     |
           |------------------|
           | + operation()    |
           +------------------+
                 /_\
                  |
        -----------------------
        |                     |
+------------------+   +----------------------+
|       Leaf       |   |       Composite      |
|------------------|   |----------------------|
| + operation()    |   | - children (based on component)|
+------------------+   | + operation()        |
                       | + add()              |
                       | + remove()           |
                       | + getChild()         |
                       +----------------------+

summary: with composite pattern we can represent a hierarchy of objects
         and treat objects on this hierarchy same way!